   "notes": "13 Trinity Street (number '13' painted over the door), Space NK apothecary. Red brick with rubbed/orange brick flat-arch window heads; ornate white painted shopfront along the whole front: Ionic pilasters, Chinese-fret panels over the doors, main glazed door at the north end (x~1.0), a second narrow glazed door in the 3rd bay (x~6.0) between multi-pane display windows, stone stallriser with basement grilles. First floor: four tall 6/6 sashes with wrought-iron balconettes; second floor: four shorter sashes (top of facade/cornice only partly in frame, so cornice type and top-floor panes are a guess). x=0 is the north end (next to no. 14, dark timber '2648' shopfront); south end abuts the yellow-brick gothic building."
